<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Longxi Commandery</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Longxi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/commandery">Commandery</a> was a commandery established by the state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> in the early 3rd century BCE in the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wei-river">Wei River</a> valley of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gansu">Gansu</a>. Retained by the Qin and Han empires, it guarded the routes to the west, and it gave its name to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/li-clan-of-longxi">Li clan of Longxi</a>, from which the Tang emperors claimed descent.</p></div>
